## Exact remaining split

### 1. Macroscopic-container branch

One actual internal inactive chamber or exterior cap has `Omega(D^2)` population/area with only `O(D)` perimeter/slack. For an internal chamber, canonical hull stability and deep matching give a protected isolate hull and isolate-only blocker graph. Proof-only §95 explains why contact creation alone need not transfer positive KKT force.

A closure must force an exact unit triangle, alter or replace the old diameter-carrying core, or construct a same-cardinality strict sub-`D` source.

### 2. Full-core branch

The preferred live bridge is no longer another carrier-decimal optimization.

On one harmonic carrier, §§120--121 convert train-direction anisotropy into local detour and then into local non-rhombic area currency. Across the whole harmonic tiling, §§122--123 give

\[
\liminf {1\over D}
\sum_r(L_r+P_{{\rm exc},r}-2d_r)
\ge {\pi\over2}(2-\sqrt3)
\]

and

\[
\sum_rP_{{\rm exc},r}\le10(e_{BB}-k).
\]

The clean source-level obstruction is therefore the aggregate outer-walk detour

\[
\boxed{\sum_r(L_r-2d_r)}
\]

coupled to `e_BB-k` and the actual diameter graph.

The new budget-floor theorem removes the full-core subbranch
\(\liminf\mu_D<1\). The promoted loaded-chord/train coupling raises the necessary
floor in the same branch to
\[
\liminf\mu_D\ge
\frac{2\pi+2\sqrt{\pi/(2\sqrt3)}}5
=1.6375621841815\ldots,
\]
but this high-surplus branch is not contradicted by the current detour/payment package.

The promoted equality-case companion `C-FULLCORE-MU-ONE-CELL` sharpens the boundary
case: if \(\mu_D\to1\), one actual attachment cell has diameter \(D-o(D)\), area
\(\pi D^2/4-o(D^2)\), and disk-shaped normalized limits, while all other cell
diameters sum to \(o(D)\). It supplies no lattice rigidity or source-preserving
deformation, so the one-cell equality closure remains open.

A closing theorem should obtain one of:

- an upper bound on that same aggregate detour strong enough to contradict §122 after the §123 payment;
- a global-minimality theorem turning the forced detour into a source-preserving strict decrease of the global diameter;
- an exact unit equilateral triangle forced directly by the carrier/loaded-hull geometry.

Further numerical improvement of `0.9762439137425688...` is secondary unless it creates one of these source-level implications.

